WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:07.020
Lovely.

2
00:00:07.070 --> 00:00:10.020
Seka, we can use «ti» now.

3
00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:11.140
We can.

4
00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:11.890
Great.

5
00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:16.890
The only thing I don't understand is why we can't go by car. Budapest is close.

6
00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:21.890
Well, Seka, look, this car is from the same year of manufacture. If it dies, there's nobody to push it.

7
00:00:21.940 --> 00:00:23.890
Oh, but I hate buses.

8
00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:26.890
Me too, but this bus is great, I can tell you, really nice.

9
00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:28.890
Because I checked: it has a great interior.

10
00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:31.890
It has Wi-Fi, air conditioning, a TV, a toilet.

11
00:00:31.940 --> 00:00:32.890
Really.

12
00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:37.070
Oh, I'll even walk, just to get a little rest from those old ladies at the nursing home.

13
00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:38.790
It's very hard with old people.

14
00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:42.170
Oh, who are you telling? I could write a textbook.

15
00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:45.450
Then drive. Let's run for our lives.

16
00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:45.850
Come on.

17
00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:50.690
Oh, the tickets.

18
00:00:55.450 --> 00:00:59.520
Oh, and we forgot the canary too. The canary.

19
00:01:49.120 --> 00:01:52.350
Please, can you give me a cloth to put on my face, I hit my head on a pole.

20
00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:53.950
Here, son, here, here.

21
00:01:56.100 --> 00:01:58.670
Where are they, damn it? They're not here.

22
00:01:58.810 --> 00:01:59.670
Here you go.

23
00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:02.040
Are you smoking?

24
00:02:02.090 --> 00:02:05.910
Come on, what's wrong with you? That comes from the neighbours.

25
00:02:05.960 --> 00:02:08.490
It's just the wind blowing like that, you know.

26
00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:15.910
No idea. Anyway, where are you going, where are you headed?

27
00:02:16.040 --> 00:02:27.320
Kalemegdan. You know what? When I was young, Kalemegdan was a neglected fortress, and you could kiss a boy there to your heart's content.

28
00:02:27.370 --> 00:02:28.970
And nobody would see you.

29
00:02:29.320 --> 00:02:29.510
Mum.

30
00:02:29.820 --> 00:02:32.470
Well listen, what do you want, I was young once.

31
00:02:33.160 --> 00:02:35.670
Baby, you have to accept that.

32
00:02:35.720 --> 00:02:39.070
Somehow you've become too possessive, you know.

33
00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:40.970
And that's not good, baby.

34
00:02:41.020 --> 00:02:45.370
Listen, Miša will come to take you to his place, you'll stay with him for three or four days.

35
00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:47.580
What would you do for three days at Kalemegdan?

36
00:02:47.630 --> 00:02:50.300
You know, let him have you for himself a bit too, understand?

37
00:02:50.350 --> 00:02:52.590
So you're not always with me, I feel sorry for him.

38
00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:55.430
But, baby, you can't manage without me.

39
00:02:55.480 --> 00:02:57.070
What will you do without me?

40
00:02:57.120 --> 00:02:58.950
You're not capable, understand?

41
00:02:59.080 --> 00:03:02.350
Well, to get used to it a little, to become independent, I'm forty years old.

42
00:03:02.600 --> 00:03:04.540
And now... What are you looking for?

43
00:03:04.590 --> 00:03:07.570
I lost something, I can't...

44
00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:11.500
Well, maybe it's better to look for something you haven't lost.

45
00:03:11.550 --> 00:03:13.150
I mean, you'd find it more easily.

46
00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:19.800
[unintelligible]

47
00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:38.770
Seka, please...

48
00:03:38.820 --> 00:03:41.090
You forgot Roza's canary.

49
00:03:41.140 --> 00:03:43.100
I did, that's why I came.

50
00:03:43.150 --> 00:03:45.120
The canary... Take it back.

51
00:03:45.170 --> 00:03:52.540
Hey neighbour, could you please look after my cat, my kitty, for just a couple of days?

52
00:03:53.440 --> 00:03:59.440
[unintelligible]

53
00:04:05.450 --> 00:04:08.410
I'd love to, neighbour, but we have a canary now.

54
00:04:08.460 --> 00:04:10.700
She won't eat it, believe me.

55
00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:15.420
Sorry, but I'm really in a hurry and travelling, I'm not here. I can't, find someone else.

56
00:04:18.510 --> 00:04:20.710
What's here, son?

57
00:04:28.370 --> 00:04:29.620
Orangutan.

58
00:04:29.670 --> 00:04:30.140
Oh.

59
00:04:33.400 --> 00:04:35.400
[unintelligible]

60
00:04:35.690 --> 00:04:39.000
Don't shout at the books, better look in your pockets.

61
00:04:39.530 --> 00:04:41.480
I did look in my pockets.

62
00:04:41.530 --> 00:04:43.630
Okay, so what are you actually looking for?

63
00:04:43.680 --> 00:04:44.060
Tickets.

64
00:04:44.110 --> 00:04:44.770
For tablić?

65
00:04:44.820 --> 00:04:45.770
For Kalemegdan.

66
00:04:45.820 --> 00:04:49.920
God, I didn't know they charge admission at Kalemegdan.

67
00:04:50.050 --> 00:04:51.120
There, the end times have come.

68
00:04:52.010 --> 00:04:55.070
Let's ask Nostradamus where the tickets are.

69
00:04:55.120 --> 00:04:55.450
Who?

70
00:04:55.500 --> 00:04:57.200
Nostradamus, man.

71
00:05:02.630 --> 00:05:05.230
He says the tickets are in the pocket.

72
00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:06.390
Oh, they're not here?

73
00:05:06.440 --> 00:05:06.820
Here.

74
00:05:06.870 --> 00:05:10.100
But these are tickets for Budapest.

75
00:05:10.250 --> 00:05:10.630
Give them to me!

76
00:05:10.680 --> 00:05:13.640
No, you're going to Kalemegdan, not to Budapest.

77
00:05:13.690 --> 00:05:14.690
Those are my tickets.

78
00:05:14.740 --> 00:05:17.950
But you said you're going to Kalemegdan, not to Budapest.

79
00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:20.780
Unless we might have sold him to the Hungarians, huh?

80
00:05:21.570 --> 00:05:23.730
Oh, listen, look at him.

81
00:05:23.780 --> 00:05:26.460
And how happy he is about the Hungarians.

82
00:05:26.510 --> 00:05:31.490
What if I change his name to Janoš or Đula, huh?

83
00:05:32.490 --> 00:05:37.090
If you don't give me the ticket, I'll put this one in a goulash.

84
00:05:38.450 --> 00:05:41.550
God, baby, what's wrong with you, why did you get so worked up?

85
00:05:41.600 --> 00:05:43.380
My life is at stake, woman.

86
00:05:48.400 --> 00:05:49.230
Hello.

87
00:05:49.280 --> 00:05:49.750
Who?

88
00:05:49.800 --> 00:05:52.070
Wait, I'm coming.

89
00:05:59.490 --> 00:06:03.640
How I once got drunk in Budapest.

90
00:06:22.620 --> 00:06:23.180
He left.

91
00:06:23.230 --> 00:06:24.820
He was some really scary guy.

92
00:06:24.870 --> 00:06:27.130
He asked me for a ride, but now he's gone.

93
00:06:27.180 --> 00:06:28.960
Look, look what I found.

94
00:06:29.010 --> 00:06:30.120
This is where you're taking me?

95
00:06:30.170 --> 00:06:32.500
Well, I'll take you to Budapest too.

96
00:06:32.550 --> 00:06:34.200
We'll go to Szentendre too.

97
00:06:34.250 --> 00:06:37.530
I just have to do one more thing, I need something...

98
00:06:37.580 --> 00:06:40.790
You look inside the house where they dance the csárdás.

99
00:06:41.020 --> 00:06:41.260
Csárdás?

100
00:06:41.310 --> 00:06:42.400
I dance the csárdás very nicely.

101
00:06:42.450 --> 00:06:43.650
But I don't know how to dance the csárdás.

102
00:06:43.700 --> 00:06:45.960
Never mind, don't worry, two left, three right and you spin.

103
00:06:46.010 --> 00:06:47.430
Then you'll see, I'll explain everything to you.

104
00:06:47.480 --> 00:06:47.890
Just a minute.

105
00:07:05.220 --> 00:07:06.970
Excuse me, do you know what time it is?

106
00:07:07.020 --> 00:07:08.130
A lot, mate, I have to...

107
00:07:08.180 --> 00:07:09.920
May I ask you something else?

108
00:07:09.970 --> 00:07:11.140
And what, what do you want to ask me?

109
00:07:11.190 --> 00:07:13.670
To explain how I get to Republic Square.

110
00:07:13.720 --> 00:07:19.220
Aha, well, fine, you come out of the building, then left, there's one traffic light, there's two, three, three, three, three...

111
00:07:19.270 --> 00:07:23.340
So at the seventh light you'll see a horseman and a horse on the right.

112
00:07:23.390 --> 00:07:25.190
Ask one of the two of them and there you go.

113
00:07:25.240 --> 00:07:26.150
Thank you very much.

114
00:07:26.360 --> 00:07:28.370
And now, a short little survey.

115
00:07:28.420 --> 00:07:28.860
About what?

116
00:07:28.910 --> 00:07:29.860
About travelling.

117
00:07:29.910 --> 00:07:31.840
Of all days, they found me today, man.

118
00:07:31.890 --> 00:07:37.380
Please, you're the first normal person since I walked into this building of yours, you know.

119
00:07:37.430 --> 00:07:42.770
Upstairs on the third floor some guy with a cat is crying like a woman, man, he drowned me.

120
00:07:42.820 --> 00:07:45.610
Please, just 15 seconds, a couple of questions.

121
00:07:45.660 --> 00:07:47.030
Fine, fine, fine.

122
00:07:48.120 --> 00:07:51.150
So, first question: where do you like to travel most?

123
00:07:51.200 --> 00:07:54.670
Is it Bali, the Seychelles, Madagascar or maybe the Maldives?

124
00:07:54.720 --> 00:07:57.190
Vrnjačka Banja, Partizanske Vode, Budva.

125
00:07:57.240 --> 00:07:59.580
I mean, what do I know, after all.

126
00:07:59.630 --> 00:08:01.840
If it's all the same to you, I'll write down Asia.

127
00:08:01.890 --> 00:08:03.350
Is that okay with you?

128
00:08:03.400 --> 00:08:04.610
Okay, okay, okay.

129
00:08:06.340 --> 00:08:09.460
Okay, what matters most to you when you travel?

130
00:08:09.510 --> 00:08:10.490
That it's cheap.

131
00:08:10.540 --> 00:08:12.180
So, under 5000 euros.

132
00:08:12.230 --> 00:08:14.830
I've never seen 5000 euros in my life.

133
00:08:15.180 --> 00:08:18.340
What means of transport do you most like to travel by?

134
00:08:18.390 --> 00:08:22.270
By bus, but I lost the tickets, mate, I can't find them anywhere.

135
00:08:22.320 --> 00:08:24.270
Since it's Asia, I'll write down by plane.

136
00:08:24.320 --> 00:08:24.630
Okay.

137
00:08:25.580 --> 00:08:26.940
Just one more question.

138
00:08:26.990 --> 00:08:29.460
So, who do you most like to travel with?

139
00:08:29.510 --> 00:08:36.080
With Seka, she's waiting for me downstairs in the car, I can't find the tickets, I'm running up and down, I can't get my bearings at all, man.

140
00:08:36.130 --> 00:08:37.740
So, family trips.

141
00:08:37.790 --> 00:08:40.130
Okay, is that it? I have no more time.

142
00:08:40.180 --> 00:08:44.180
Just one more thing, if it's not a problem, a phone number, they won't accept my survey otherwise.

143
00:08:44.230 --> 00:08:45.710
Well, make something up, man.

144
00:08:48.990 --> 00:08:53.820
Budapest, goulash, sataraš, Budapest, Budapest.

145
00:08:56.950 --> 00:08:57.580
What are you doing?

146
00:08:57.630 --> 00:09:00.300
We're practising, Janoš and I are practising Hungarian.

147
00:09:00.350 --> 00:09:02.670
But that's not a cockatoo, it's a canary.

148
00:09:02.720 --> 00:09:03.420
Never mind.

149
00:09:03.570 --> 00:09:05.230
Please, give me the tickets.

150
00:09:05.280 --> 00:09:07.550
Milentije, son, be serious.

151
00:09:07.600 --> 00:09:08.440
What's wrong with you?

152
00:09:08.490 --> 00:09:09.930
Kalemegdan is close.

153
00:09:09.980 --> 00:09:14.850
You're surely not going to Kalemegdan via Budapest, God forbid.

154
00:09:14.900 --> 00:09:18.280
Roza, I'm not going to Kalemegdan, I'm going to Budapest.

155
00:09:18.850 --> 00:09:19.720
Mm, so that's how it is.

156
00:09:19.770 --> 00:09:26.060
I lied to you, I lied to Miša so he'd come to look after you, but that's the only way I can get away for a couple of days.

157
00:09:26.910 --> 00:09:27.720
Shame on you.

158
00:09:27.770 --> 00:09:28.990
Shame on me, I know.

159
00:09:29.040 --> 00:09:29.580
You're going alone?

160
00:09:29.630 --> 00:09:30.980
What about the girlfriend?

161
00:09:31.870 --> 00:09:34.290
Why didn't you introduce me to the girlfriend?

162
00:09:34.340 --> 00:09:38.510
You've met a little, but never mind, I can't talk to you now, please.

163
00:09:38.560 --> 00:09:41.690
Please, give me those tickets, I'll be away only three days.

164
00:09:41.740 --> 00:09:43.390
How three, you said a couple?

165
00:09:43.440 --> 00:09:44.680
Well, two nights, three days.

166
00:09:44.730 --> 00:09:47.500
I know, but three is one thing and a couple is another, oh dear.

167
00:09:47.950 --> 00:09:50.780
You know what, you've always been like that, even as a kid.

168
00:09:50.830 --> 00:09:54.460
Do you remember claiming that two hands have eleven fingers?

169
00:09:54.510 --> 00:09:54.800
How?

170
00:09:54.850 --> 00:09:56.810
Well, like this. You say it like this:

171
00:09:56.860 --> 00:10:00.560
Ten, nine, eight, seven, six, and five, that's eleven.

172
00:10:21.680 --> 00:10:27.180
Oh, damn, damn, baby, one day you'll set the house on fire too.

173
00:10:27.700 --> 00:10:31.700
[unintelligible]

174
00:10:32.680 --> 00:10:34.880
Coming, coming! A minute!

175
00:10:51.440 --> 00:10:54.100
[unintelligible]

176
00:10:54.600 --> 00:10:55.750
So, are we going?

177
00:10:55.800 --> 00:10:57.330
We are. In about ten minutes.

178
00:10:57.380 --> 00:10:59.020
I have some family problems.

179
00:10:59.070 --> 00:11:00.550
Are you hiding something from me?

180
00:11:00.620 --> 00:11:04.300
[unintelligible]

181
00:11:04.600 --> 00:11:04.860
How?

182
00:11:04.910 --> 00:11:07.550
Just, please, just a minute. I'll be right there.

183
00:11:10.900 --> 00:11:14.600
[unintelligible]

184
00:11:19.870 --> 00:11:22.140
Roza, is everything all right?

185
00:11:27.400 --> 00:11:29.350
[unintelligible]

186
00:11:29.400 --> 00:11:33.200
I don't get why I'm drinking this water when I'm not thirsty at all.

187
00:11:33.400 --> 00:11:36.200
That's why, Ros! To put out the fire!

188
00:11:36.760 --> 00:11:40.020
I forgot to tell you, Miša called.

189
00:11:40.070 --> 00:11:42.310
How much he cares about me, yes.

190
00:11:42.360 --> 00:11:45.710
Yes, from the depths of his selfless soul.

191
00:11:46.420 --> 00:11:48.420
[unintelligible]

192
00:11:48.760 --> 00:11:49.840
Give me the tickets.

193
00:11:49.890 --> 00:11:56.100
Come on, come with me, please, to talk seriously like mature people.

194
00:11:56.150 --> 00:11:57.760
Roza, give me the tickets!

195
00:11:57.810 --> 00:11:58.190
Mum!

196
00:11:58.240 --> 00:12:02.100
Please, give me the tickets, my bus will leave!

197
00:12:02.150 --> 00:12:06.020
Calm down, please, baby, come on, lie down on the couch.

198
00:12:06.070 --> 00:12:08.370
Oh God, all right, all right, I'll lie down.

199
00:12:08.420 --> 00:12:10.890
There, I'm lying down, give me the tickets!

200
00:12:11.160 --> 00:12:12.730
Relax, you have a problem.

201
00:12:12.780 --> 00:12:14.290
Exactly, I do, give me the tickets.

202
00:12:14.780 --> 00:12:22.830
Janoš, sorry, please, this will now be a psychoanalytic session, and I'll call you Freud afterwards.

203
00:12:23.750 --> 00:12:29.770
So the problem isn't the tickets, son, the problem is in your subconscious.

204
00:12:30.340 --> 00:12:31.460
Mum, give me the ticket.

205
00:12:31.510 --> 00:12:34.550
Listen, since I finished studying psychology...

206
00:12:34.620 --> 00:12:36.250
[unintelligible]

207
00:12:36.300 --> 00:12:39.360
That's not the topic at all right now, you understand, not the topic.

208
00:12:39.410 --> 00:12:46.710
I can conclude that you have a problem with your alter ego, your superego, your subconscious and generally with yourself.

209
00:12:46.760 --> 00:12:49.110
Mum, give me the ticket. Wait, sorry.

210
00:12:49.700 --> 00:12:55.700
[unintelligible]

211
00:13:01.940 --> 00:13:04.300
When did that first happen?

212
00:13:05.350 --> 00:13:06.460
Give me the ticket, woman!

213
00:13:06.650 --> 00:13:14.400
We have to work on honesty, because, listen, that's something we missed in our growing up together.

214
00:13:14.950 --> 00:13:20.300
So please relax, close your eyes, answer the questions, and I'll take notes.

215
00:13:21.890 --> 00:13:22.250
Baby!

216
00:13:22.300 --> 00:13:24.140
Give me the tickets, please.

217
00:13:24.770 --> 00:13:29.130
We start with the simplest question. How old are you?

218
00:13:29.180 --> 00:13:31.040
Forty. How old are you?

219
00:13:31.090 --> 00:13:32.800
That's not the topic at all right now.

220
00:13:34.810 --> 00:13:35.870
What's your name?

221
00:13:35.920 --> 00:13:38.340
You and Dad gave me my name, Ros.

222
00:13:38.390 --> 00:13:43.120
Please, baby, get serious, close your eyes, this is a scientific procedure.

223
00:13:43.530 --> 00:13:44.950
What do you feel?

224
00:13:45.000 --> 00:13:49.300
I feel nervous, I feel I'm going to explode.

225
00:13:50.860 --> 00:13:54.680
[unintelligible]

226
00:13:56.820 --> 00:13:57.810
You're impossible.

227
00:13:57.860 --> 00:14:00.490
What am I like? Give me, please, give me the tickets.

228
00:14:00.640 --> 00:14:02.100
Miša will come to look after you.

229
00:14:02.150 --> 00:14:04.440
Come on, tell me, please, who are you going with?

230
00:14:04.490 --> 00:14:07.010
With Seka. Her name is Seka, she works at a nursing home.

231
00:14:07.080 --> 00:14:10.360
Oh, don't, don't, please, don't mention that institution to me.

232
00:14:10.410 --> 00:14:11.090
Don't, don't.

233
00:14:11.160 --> 00:14:13.490
Please, Roza, give me the tickets, what does it cost you?

234
00:14:16.440 --> 00:14:17.930
Miša will come to look after you.

235
00:14:17.980 --> 00:14:19.810
I'm not a puppy that somebody has to look after.

236
00:14:19.860 --> 00:14:23.340
I'm not a puppy, I'm a person who needs love and attention.

237
00:14:23.390 --> 00:14:27.610
Believe it or not, I'm also a person who needs love and attention.

238
00:14:27.660 --> 00:14:30.340
There, believe it or not, I like being loved too.

239
00:14:30.390 --> 00:14:32.560
Please, Mum, please, Miša will come.

240
00:14:32.610 --> 00:14:34.210
I'll be away only three days.

241
00:14:34.260 --> 00:14:40.190
You'll play a bit there with the kids, here you'll go to waste with this Hungarian mutt and everyone will be great, there.

242
00:14:40.240 --> 00:14:44.090
That's a classic example of overexcitement.

243
00:14:50.430 --> 00:14:50.950
Hello?

244
00:14:51.000 --> 00:14:53.120
What? What Syrian?

245
00:14:53.170 --> 00:14:57.090
Wait, wait, here I am, coming down, coming down!

246
00:15:11.080 --> 00:15:12.940
[unintelligible]

247
00:15:13.100 --> 00:15:17.000
If I knew how to drive, I'd have taken him straight to that Kragujevac

248
00:15:17.100 --> 00:15:18.000
where he asked me to take him.

249
00:15:18.100 --> 00:15:20.000
That man crossed himself with both his left and right hand and said:

250
00:15:20.100 --> 00:15:22.000
only in Serbia do taxi drivers not know how to drive.

251
00:15:22.500 --> 00:15:24.510
Are we going or not?

252
00:15:24.560 --> 00:15:26.830
We're going, but I've misplaced a ticket somewhere.

253
00:15:26.880 --> 00:15:27.160
Oh...

254
00:15:27.210 --> 00:15:30.950
Just a minute, please, I only came to tell you, and we're going.

255
00:15:32.200 --> 00:15:34.150
[unintelligible]

256
00:15:34.200 --> 00:15:36.000
Oh, my sister!

257
00:15:36.200 --> 00:15:38.000
Who did you find to dance the csárdás with?

258
00:15:38.780 --> 00:15:40.490
Three left, three right and a turn.

259
00:15:43.320 --> 00:15:45.900
It's me, Mum, open up!

260
00:15:46.570 --> 00:15:47.750
And who is «me»?

261
00:15:47.800 --> 00:15:51.350
It's me, baby, Milentije, your son.

262
00:15:54.200 --> 00:15:59.200
[unintelligible]

263
00:16:00.980 --> 00:16:02.790
Mum, please, open up!

264
00:16:02.840 --> 00:16:05.950
If you don't say the code, I'm calling the police.

265
00:16:07.200 --> 00:16:13.200
[unintelligible]

266
00:16:23.020 --> 00:16:24.480
Open up, Roza!

267
00:16:24.530 --> 00:16:27.020
We'll change the code.

268
00:16:27.070 --> 00:16:33.620
Well, son, but when you moved into the flat, you chose that code yourself.

269
00:16:35.640 --> 00:16:37.790
To hell with the code!

270
00:16:37.840 --> 00:16:44.950
Don't, please, baby, that woman is a bad influence on you, now you lie like a dog and you've started swearing too.

271
00:16:45.000 --> 00:16:46.290
Roza, give me the tickets!

272
00:16:46.340 --> 00:16:50.850
I don't know, son, I don't know how to give them to you, don't, don't, what do I do?

273
00:16:50.900 --> 00:16:54.860
I've lived with you all my life, you drove my ex-wife out of here.

274
00:16:54.910 --> 00:16:55.490
Me? God!

275
00:16:55.540 --> 00:16:58.790
I have to go on that trip, did you hear me?

276
00:16:58.840 --> 00:17:00.790
Don't, we could also travel together.

277
00:17:02.840 --> 00:17:04.790
Roza, give, give me those tickets!

278
00:17:04.840 --> 00:17:07.600
[unintelligible]

279
00:17:07.680 --> 00:17:10.010
Oh God, don't be afraid, don't be afraid, don't be afraid.

280
00:17:10.500 --> 00:17:14.350
And you don't know how hard it is to be a parent.

281
00:17:14.510 --> 00:17:18.290
Oh God, I don't know where I went wrong.

282
00:17:18.420 --> 00:17:22.500
And you see, somehow Miša turned out great.

283
00:17:22.750 --> 00:17:28.470
He's mature and university-educated, a famous surgeon, yes.

284
00:17:29.400 --> 00:17:30.410
Oh God.

285
00:17:34.540 --> 00:17:36.440
The doorbell's ringing.

286
00:17:36.890 --> 00:17:41.790
What's going on? What happened? Where's the fire? What's going on?

287
00:17:47.060 --> 00:17:48.760
[unintelligible]

288
00:17:49.280 --> 00:17:50.870
Listen, I have a big problem.

289
00:17:50.920 --> 00:17:51.220
Okay.

290
00:17:51.270 --> 00:17:55.090
Look, I have to go to Budapest for four days with a girl, you understand?

291
00:17:55.140 --> 00:17:55.440
Okay.

292
00:17:55.490 --> 00:17:57.900
And she's waiting for me downstairs in the car, and she's gorgeous.

293
00:17:57.950 --> 00:17:58.260
Okay.

294
00:17:58.310 --> 00:18:02.890
And I can't do it because I'm running up and down here and treating Mum, you understand?

295
00:18:02.940 --> 00:18:03.240
Okay.

296
00:18:03.290 --> 00:18:08.570
And I don't have time and I can't find the tickets for Budapest because she hid them somewhere here.

297
00:18:09.440 --> 00:18:10.530
Where is the girl waiting for you?

298
00:18:10.580 --> 00:18:11.040
In the car!

299
00:18:11.090 --> 00:18:12.700
Did you say gorgeous girl?

300
00:18:12.750 --> 00:18:14.070
Gorgeous, brother, gorgeous.

301
00:18:14.120 --> 00:18:14.920
You know how beautiful.

302
00:18:14.970 --> 00:18:16.690
Why are you torturing yourself? Relax, hey.

303
00:18:17.060 --> 00:18:19.270
I'm your older brother, right?

304
00:18:19.320 --> 00:18:19.580
Yes.

305
00:18:19.630 --> 00:18:21.110
I'm here to help you.

306
00:18:21.160 --> 00:18:21.420
You are.

307
00:18:21.470 --> 00:18:22.820
Okay, I'll help you.

308
00:18:22.870 --> 00:18:24.170
Thank you so much, brother.

309
00:18:24.540 --> 00:18:25.710
Where are you going? Stop.

310
00:18:25.760 --> 00:18:29.860
You take care of Mum here, and I'll step in for the girl.

311
00:18:29.910 --> 00:18:33.110
Everything will be fine. Hey, take it easy.

312
00:18:50.100 --> 00:18:50.900
Why did you come?

313
00:18:50.950 --> 00:18:54.410
I'm begging you, neighbour, I have nobody to leave my kitty with.

314
00:18:54.700 --> 00:19:00.700
[unintelligible]

315
00:19:27.560 --> 00:19:29.310
Who are you?

316
00:19:38.690 --> 00:19:40.590
And who are you?

317
00:19:52.040 --> 00:19:53.940
I'm Seka.

318
00:20:06.680 --> 00:20:11.510
Seka, I have one... let's say, sad piece of news for you.

319
00:20:15.370 --> 00:20:19.740
Well, give me the sad one first, so we can rejoice afterwards.

320
00:20:23.100 --> 00:20:27.910
[unintelligible]

321
00:20:27.960 --> 00:20:30.200
He won't come.

322
00:20:30.320 --> 00:20:32.000
He won't? I knew it.

323
00:20:34.860 --> 00:20:36.900
That's sad news.

324
00:20:39.680 --> 00:20:41.810
And what's the happy one?

325
00:20:41.860 --> 00:20:46.160
My younger brother sent me to replace him.

326
00:20:46.410 --> 00:20:47.400
Who are you?

327
00:20:48.070 --> 00:20:50.350
Professor Popović.

328
00:20:50.980 --> 00:20:52.130
A surgeon?

329
00:20:52.180 --> 00:20:54.680
Well yes, a real one.

330
00:20:55.610 --> 00:21:00.060
I fulfil the aesthetic wishes of my clients.

331
00:21:10.430 --> 00:21:13.900
As far as I can see, there's nothing wrong with you.

332
00:21:14.120 --> 00:21:15.300
Oh, thank you.

333
00:21:15.350 --> 00:21:16.980
You mean on the outside?

334
00:21:17.030 --> 00:21:21.700
For the inside I'd have to get to know you a bit better.

335
00:21:22.510 --> 00:21:25.150
I don't know, maybe for the better.

336
00:21:25.200 --> 00:21:29.800
We could perhaps round these cheekbones a little.

337
00:21:34.450 --> 00:21:36.950
Like Khloé Kardashian.

338
00:21:38.300 --> 00:21:40.270
No. Prettier.

339
00:21:40.800 --> 00:21:43.970
Then you really are a good surgeon.

340
00:21:46.390 --> 00:21:49.570
And do you know how to dance the csárdás?

341
00:21:52.000 --> 00:21:55.000
[unintelligible]

342
00:22:00.940 --> 00:22:05.350
I'll nicely chop you into pieces and sell you to a Chinese restaurant!

343
00:22:05.400 --> 00:22:06.970
But Janoš is under stress!

344
00:22:07.020 --> 00:22:10.880
I don't care, when I catch this one I'll slaughter him!

345
00:22:10.930 --> 00:22:14.930
Don't, what will neighbour Mađarević say if you kill his cat.

346
00:22:14.980 --> 00:22:19.250
What will he say to me, he'll say thanks, thank you, that's what he'll say.

347
00:22:19.300 --> 00:22:19.930
Oh, the cat!

348
00:22:22.000 --> 00:22:24.800
Oh, Miša, I can't talk now, please, I'll call you back.

349
00:22:25.000 --> 00:22:26.000
Kitty, kitty!

350
00:22:28.930 --> 00:22:36.080
Rozalija on the phone. Miša, son, that brother of yours is nervous, he's chasing some cat, yes.

351
00:22:38.180 --> 00:22:41.880
Aha, okay, okay, son, I'll tell him.

352
00:22:42.230 --> 00:22:45.630
And when will you come to visit me?

353
00:22:45.840 --> 00:22:48.270
Aha, on Sunday. Okay.

354
00:22:48.320 --> 00:22:50.190
Come on, lovely. Bye.

355
00:22:50.240 --> 00:22:51.770
Bye, bye, bye.

356
00:22:51.820 --> 00:22:52.220
Bye.

357
00:22:52.980 --> 00:22:54.840
[unintelligible]

358
00:22:54.890 --> 00:22:55.970
What happened?

359
00:22:56.020 --> 00:23:02.640
Listen, Miša told you not to worry about anything, that he sorted everything out with the cat.

360
00:23:03.090 --> 00:23:05.200
I haven't caught the cat.

361
00:23:05.250 --> 00:23:09.070
Not this cat, but some cat in the car.

362
00:23:09.120 --> 00:23:14.240
He drove her off for two nights, three days, and I pay for them.

363
00:23:17.600 --> 00:23:23.600
[unintelligible]

364
00:23:58.880 --> 00:24:00.320
Take her to Miša.

365
00:24:00.370 --> 00:24:03.410
Who will, for whom, if not one's own for one's own.

366
00:24:15.680 --> 00:24:18.440
Miša isn't answering these days.

367
00:24:18.490 --> 00:24:19.940
I wonder why.

368
00:24:19.990 --> 00:24:25.940
Jovanka says he went to some conference in Vrnjačka Banja.

369
00:24:26.620 --> 00:24:28.470
Two nights, three days.

370
00:24:28.520 --> 00:24:30.480
Three. Ah, poor Miša.

371
00:24:31.470 --> 00:24:32.430
Poor me?

372
00:24:32.480 --> 00:24:37.230
Baby, let's you and I take a walk around Kalemegdan.

373
00:24:38.070 --> 00:24:44.390
From what I see in this cup, I shouldn't even leave the house.

374
00:24:46.010 --> 00:24:46.400
Why?

375
00:24:46.450 --> 00:24:50.380
A tram will hit me for sure. Look.

376
00:24:50.810 --> 00:24:54.510
No, no, don't worry, that's not a tram.

377
00:24:54.840 --> 00:24:55.240
Here?

378
00:24:55.290 --> 00:24:57.250
Well, that's a bus.

379
00:25:00.350 --> 00:25:04.420
I was young once, understand? Oh God!

380
00:25:12.500 --> 00:25:15.500
[unintelligible]

381
00:25:26.500 --> 00:25:31.400
We can share a sad piece of news and a very, very happy one.

382
00:25:43.200 --> 00:25:47.500
I have to go on that trip, give me that ticket!

383
00:25:47.640 --> 00:25:50.400
We could travel somewhere together, we could!

384
00:25:50.460 --> 00:25:51.950
Stop, Rosa, stop, Rosa!

385
00:25:52.360 --> 00:25:56.480
[unintelligible]

386
00:25:58.640 --> 00:26:01.400
So what are you staring at me for?
